#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:3
msgid "気体の種類が違っても、1 molの体積はほぼ同じ？"
msgstr "Do Different Gases Have Nearly the Same Volume per Mole?"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:5
msgid ""
"水素は軽く、二酸化炭素は重い気体です。\\ それでも高校の化学では、同じ温度と圧力なら、どちらも1 molの体積はほぼ同じだと習います。\\ "
"重い分子と軽い分子の違いは、どこへ行くのでしょうか。"
msgstr ""
"Hydrogen is a light gas and carbon dioxide is a heavy one. \\ Yet in high"
" school chemistry, we learn that a mole of either gas occupies nearly the"
" same volume at the same temperature and pressure. \\ Where does the "
"difference between light and heavy molecules show up?"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:9
msgid ""
"前回の :doc:`argon_molar_volume` では、Arの体積を変えて圧力を調べました。\\ "
"今回はセルの大きさと分子数をそろえ、気体の種類だけを変えて、分子の速さと圧力を比べてみましょう。"
msgstr ""
"In the previous part, :doc:`argon_molar_volume`, we examined how pressure"
" changes with the volume of Ar. \\ Here we keep the cell size and number "
"of molecules the same and vary only the gas species to compare molecular "
"speeds and pressures."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:13
msgid "計算対象と計算条件"
msgstr "Systems and Calculation Conditions"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:15
msgid ""
"今回比較するのは、H₂、N₂、O₂、Ar、CO₂の5種類です。\\ 使った分子モデルを :numref:`fig-five-gas-models`"
" に示します。\\ Arは1原子が1個の気体粒子に相当するので、ここでは他の気体と合わせて粒子数を「分子数」と呼びます。"
msgstr ""
"We compare five gases: H₂, N₂, O₂, Ar, and CO₂. \\ The molecular models "
"are shown in :numref:`fig-five-gas-models`. \\ Each Ar atom counts as one"
" gas particle. We use “number of molecules” for the particle count across"
" all five gases."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:24
msgid ""
"各気体の440 ps時点の保存座標から代表1分子を取り出し、分子の平面を紙面に合わせて回転した図です。\\ "
"結合距離の表示スケールは5種で共通です。球の半径は表示用の0.022 nmで、原子の物理的な大きさを表しません。\\ "
"右の数値はモデルの原子質量を足したモル質量（g/mol）です。\\ "
"CO₂の登録モデルは角度が少し曲がれるので、図も保存座標の曲がりをそのまま描いています。"
msgstr ""
"The figure shows one representative molecule of each gas from the "
"coordinates saved at 440 ps, with the molecular plane rotated into the "
"plane of the figure. \\ Bond distances are drawn to the same scale for "
"all five gases. Spheres have a display radius of 0.022 nm and do not "
"represent the physical sizes of the atoms. \\ The values on the right are"
" molar masses (g/mol), obtained by summing the atomic masses in each "
"model. \\ The registered CO₂ model allows the angle to bend slightly, so "
"the figure also shows the bend in the saved coordinates as it is."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:29
msgid ""
"条件を :numref:`tab-five-gas-conditions` にまとめます。\\ "
"H₂・N₂・O₂を2,000原子にするのは、1,000分子をそろえるためです。\\ "
"原子数を全部1,000個にそろえてしまうと、気体粒子の数が変わります。"
msgstr ""
":numref:`tab-five-gas-conditions` summarizes the conditions. \\ We use "
"2,000 atoms each for H₂, N₂, and O₂ to give 1,000 molecules of each gas. "
"\\ Using 1,000 atoms for every gas would give different numbers of gas "
"particles."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:33
msgid "5気体の比較条件"
msgstr "Conditions for comparing the five gases"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:39
msgid "項目"
msgstr "Item"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:40
msgid "条件"
msgstr "Conditions"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:41
msgid "分子数"
msgstr "Number of molecules"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:42
msgid "各1,000。原子数はAr：1,000、H₂・N₂・O₂：各2,000、CO₂：3,000"
msgstr ""
"1,000 each, with 1,000 atoms for Ar, 2,000 each for H₂, N₂, and O₂, and "
"3,000 for CO₂"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:43
msgid "温度・セル"
msgstr "Temperature and cell"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:44
msgid "273.15 K、一辺33.3879144 nmの立方体、3方向周期境界"
msgstr ""
"273.15 K, cubic cell 33.3879144 nm on a side, periodic boundary "
"conditions in all three directions"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:45
msgid "計算方法"
msgstr "Calculation method"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:46
msgid "GROMACS 2026.2標準混合精度版、WSLローカルCPU、NVT、確率的動力学による温度制御"
msgstr ""
"Standard mixed-precision GROMACS 2026.2, local CPU on WSL, NVT, "
"temperature control by stochastic dynamics"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:47
msgid "時間刻み"
msgstr "Time step"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:48
msgid "H₂：0.5 fs、ほかの4種：2 fs"
msgstr "0.5 fs for H₂, 2 fs for the other four gases"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:49
msgid "測定区間"
msgstr "Production period"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:50
msgid "全440 psのうち40 psより後の400 ps。各3シード"
msgstr "400 ps after the first 40 ps of the 440 ps run. Three seeds for each gas"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:51
msgid "分子内の運動"
msgstr "Intramolecular motion"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:52
msgid "H₂・N₂・O₂は結合長を拘束。CO₂はC–Oを2本拘束し、角度には調和ポテンシャル"
msgstr ""
"Bond lengths constrained for H₂, N₂, and O₂. Two C–O bonds constrained "
"and a harmonic potential for the bond angle in CO₂"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:54
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"計算には、それぞれの気体についてQuloudに登録されているモデルを使います。\\ "
"とくにCO₂は文献の完全剛体TraPPEから変更されたモデルです。\\ 温度制御は、第1回のV-"
"rescaleではなく、各原子に熱浴を作用させる確率的動力学（SD）にしました。\\ その理由は :numref:`{number}. "
"{name} <gas-five-thermostat>` で説明します。\\ モデルと数値条件の詳細、Quloudの標準設定との差は "
":doc:`reproduction` にまとめています。"
msgstr ""
"We use the models registered in Quloud for each gas. \\ In particular, "
"the CO₂ model is a modification of the fully rigid TraPPE model from the "
"literature. \\ For temperature control, we used stochastic dynamics (SD),"
" which applies a heat bath to each atom, instead of the V-rescale method "
"used in Part 1. \\ The reason is explained in :numref:`{number}. {name} "
"<gas-five-thermostat>`. \\ The model details, numerical settings, and "
"departures from the standard Quloud settings are documented in "
":doc:`reproduction`."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:61
msgid "分子の重心速度"
msgstr "Molecular Center-of-Mass Velocity"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:63
msgid ""
"軽い気体の分子は、重い気体の分子より速く動くと予想されます。\\ "
"ただし、H₂やCO₂の原子の速度には、分子全体の移動に加えて回転や内部の動きも混ざります。\\ "
"そこで、分子ごとに原子の速度を質量で重み付けし、分子全体の重心の速度を取り出します。"
msgstr ""
"We expect molecules of lighter gases to move faster than those of heavier"
" gases. \\ However, the velocities of the atoms in H₂ or CO₂ include "
"rotation and internal motion as well as translation of the whole "
"molecule. \\ For each molecule, we therefore take the mass-weighted "
"average of the atomic velocities to obtain its center-of-mass velocity."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:67
msgid ""
"速さを比べる指標には、重心速度の二乗を分子と時刻について平均した後に平方根を取る、\\ 二乗平均平方根速度 "
":math:`v_{\\mathrm{rms}}` を使います。\\ 理想気体の理論式は、モル質量 :math:`M` "
"をkg/molで表すと次のようになります。"
msgstr ""
"To compare speeds, we average the squared magnitude of the center-of-mass"
" velocity over molecules and time \\ and take the square root to obtain "
"the root-mean-square speed :math:`v_{\\mathrm{rms}}`. \\ For an ideal "
"gas, with molar mass :math:`M` in kg/mol, this is given by"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:71
msgid ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"v_{\\mathrm{rms}}&=\\sqrt{\\langle|\\boldsymbol{v}_{\\mathrm{COM}}|^2\\rangle}\\\\"
"\n"
"&=\\sqrt{\\frac{3RT}{M}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"v_{\\mathrm{rms}}&=\\sqrt{\\langle|\\boldsymbol{v}_{\\mathrm{COM}}|^2\\rangle}\\\\"
"\n"
"&=\\sqrt{\\frac{3RT}{M}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:79
msgid ""
"理論値とMDの測定値を :numref:`tab-five-gas-speeds` と :numref:`fig-five-gas-speeds`"
" で比較します。\\ 理論値にはモデルが持つ原子質量の合計を用いており、MDの速度から理論線を調整してはいません。"
msgstr ""
":numref:`tab-five-gas-speeds` and :numref:`fig-five-gas-speeds` compare "
"the theoretical values and MD measurements. \\ The theoretical values use"
" the sum of the atomic masses in each model. The MD velocities were not "
"used to adjust the theoretical curve."

