#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:95
msgid ""
"横軸はモル質量（g/mol）、縦軸は分子重心の二乗平均平方根速度（m/s）です。\\ 点と誤差棒は :numref:`tab-five-gas-"
"speeds` のMD平均と1標準誤差、曲線は式 :eq:`eq-gas-speed` による273.15 Kの事前予測です。\\ "
"速さは、出力に保存された各原子の速度から分子ごとに重心速度を求めて計算しています。\\ "
"原子ごとの速さや、保存座標の差分から求めた値ではありません。"
msgstr ""
"The horizontal axis shows molar mass (g/mol), and the vertical axis shows"
" the root-mean-square speed of the molecular center of mass (m/s). \\ "
"Points and error bars show the MD means and one standard error from "
":numref:`tab-five-gas-speeds`, and the curve is the a priori prediction "
"at 273.15 K from Equation :eq:`eq-gas-speed`. \\ The speeds are "
"calculated from the center-of-mass velocity of each molecule, obtained "
"from the atomic velocities saved in the output. \\ They are not atomic "
"speeds or values obtained from differences of the saved coordinates."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:100
msgid ""
"MDの速さは、どの気体でも理論値と0.1%以内で一致しました。\\ 最も軽いH₂は約1,840 m/s、最も重いCO₂は約390 "
"m/sで、軽い分子ほど速く、重い分子ほどゆっくり動きます。\\ "
"ただし、今回の温度制御は各原子に温度に応じた揺らぎを直接与え、熱平衡の速度分布へ近づける方法です [2]_ 。\\ "
"この一致は、そのように作った分布から分子全体の運動を正しく取り出せることを確認したものです。\\ "
"分子どうしの衝突だけで、この関係が生まれる過程を独立に示したものではありません。"
msgstr ""
"The MD speeds agreed with the theoretical values to within 0.1% for every"
" gas. \\ The lightest gas, H₂, moves at about 1,840 m/s and the heaviest,"
" CO₂, at about 390 m/s: lighter molecules move faster and heavier ones "
"move more slowly. \\ However, the temperature control used here applies "
"temperature-dependent fluctuations directly to each atom to bring the "
"velocities toward a thermal equilibrium distribution [2]_. \\ This "
"agreement confirms that the motion of whole molecules can be correctly "
"extracted from a distribution generated in this way. \\ It does not "
"independently show how this relationship arises from collisions between "
"molecules alone."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:107
msgid "圧力とアボガドロの法則"
msgstr "Pressure and Avogadro’s Law"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:109
msgid ""
"では、速さがこれだけ違う分子を同じ数だけ入れたとき、圧力はどうなるでしょうか。\\ セルの一辺33.3879144 "
"nmは、第1回と同じく、理想気体ならちょうど1 atmになる大きさです。\\ 理想気体の予測は1.01325 bar（1 atm）です。\\ "
"MDの圧力は、速度から理想気体の式で作るのではなく、GROMACSのEDRに保存された ``Pressure`` を直接読み取ります。\\ 結果を"
" :numref:`fig-five-gas-pressure` に示します。"
msgstr ""
"So what happens to the pressure when we put equal numbers of molecules "
"with such different speeds into the cell? \\ As in Part 1, the cell side "
"length of 33.3879144 nm is the size at which an ideal gas would be at "
"exactly 1 atm. \\ The ideal gas prediction is 1.01325 bar (1 atm). \\ We "
"read the MD pressure directly from the ``Pressure`` entry saved in the "
"GROMACS EDR file, rather than deriving it from the velocities with the "
"ideal gas equation. \\ The results are shown in :numref:`fig-five-gas-"
"pressure`."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:120
msgid ""
"横軸は5種類の気体、縦軸は圧力（bar）です。\\ "
"塗りつぶした丸は標準混合精度、白抜きの四角は倍精度の参考計算による各3シードのSD平均です。\\ "
"横位置を少しずらして示しています。誤差棒は1統計標準誤差で、この表示幅ではほぼ記号の中に収まります。\\ 時間刻みはどちらもH₂が0.5 "
"fs、ほかは2 fsです。拘束を解く方法LINCSの設定は、CO₂では混合精度が次数4・反復1、倍精度が次数8・反復2です。\\ "
"倍精度版はQuloudの標準環境とは異なるローカル検証用の実行環境です。\\ 破線は理想気体の予測1.01325 "
"barです。圧力の全体の大きさを比べるため、縦軸を0から表示しています。\\ "
"気体ごとの微小な差の数値収束は確認できていないため、拡大した比較は行いません。"
msgstr ""
"The horizontal axis shows the five gases, and the vertical axis shows "
"pressure (bar). \\ Filled circles show standard mixed-precision results "
"and open squares show double-precision reference results, each the SD "
"mean over three seeds. \\ The points are slightly offset horizontally. "
"The error bars show one statistical standard error and mostly fit within "
"the markers at this scale. \\ Both sets use a time step of 0.5 fs for H₂ "
"and 2 fs for the other gases. For CO₂, LINCS, the method used to solve "
"the constraints, uses order 4 and one iteration in mixed precision and "
"order 8 and two iterations in double precision. \\ The double-precision "
"version is a local validation environment that differs from Quloud’s "
"standard environment. \\ The dashed line marks the ideal gas prediction "
"of 1.01325 bar. The vertical axis starts at zero so that the overall "
"pressure magnitudes can be compared. \\ We do not show a zoomed "
"comparison because numerical convergence of the small differences between"
" gases has not been confirmed."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:128
msgid ""
"分子の速さが大きく違っても、 :numref:`tab-five-gas-conditions` "
"の時間刻みで計算した圧力は1.0126〜1.0206 barで、5種類とも理想気体の予測から1%以内でした。\\ "
"倍精度の参考計算（白抜きの四角）でも、5種類とも1%以内でした。\\ 各気体の値は :numref:`tab-precision-"
"reference` に載せています。\\ "
"これは、同じ温度と圧力で同じ体積の気体に含まれる分子数が等しいという、アボガドロの法則の考え方につながります。\\ "
"ここでは体積を固定して圧力を比べたので、各気体について1 atmの体積そのものをフィットしたわけではありません。"
msgstr ""
"Even though molecular speeds differ greatly, the pressures calculated "
"with the time steps in :numref:`tab-five-gas-conditions` were "
"1.0126–1.0206 bar, within 1% of the ideal gas prediction for all five "
"gases. \\ The double-precision reference calculations (open squares) were"
" also within 1% for all five gases. \\ The values for each gas are listed"
" in :numref:`tab-precision-reference`. \\ This connects to the idea "
"behind Avogadro’s law: equal volumes of gases at the same temperature and"
" pressure contain equal numbers of molecules. \\ Here we fixed the volume"
" and compared pressures, so we did not fit the volume at 1 atm itself for"
" each gas."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:134
msgid ""
"ただし、この「1%以内」は採用した時間刻みでの結果です。\\ "
"拘束のある分子では、GROMACSの標準の混合精度版（計算の多くを単精度で行う）で時間刻みを小さくすると、計算上の誤差で圧力が高くなる条件がありました。\\"
" H₂を0.25 fsにすると理想値から約+2.7%、CO₂を1 fsにすると約+7.3%になり、「1%以内」から外れます（ :numref"
":`tab-mixed-timestep` ）。\\ "
"H₂の倍精度では刻みを半分にした対照とも統計誤差の範囲で一致していますが、混合精度の圧力の収束を保証する結果ではありません。\\ "
"1%未満の違いも精度や拘束の計算条件で変わるため、気体ごとの性質の差とは考えません。\\ 数値と対照条件は :doc:`reproduction`"
" にまとめています。"
msgstr ""
"However, this “within 1%” result applies to the time steps we adopted. \\"
" For molecules with constraints, there were conditions under which "
"reducing the time step in the standard mixed-precision version of GROMACS"
" (which performs most calculations in single precision) increased the "
"pressure through numerical error. \\ With 0.25 fs for H₂, the pressure "
"was about +2.7% from the ideal value, and with 1 fs for CO₂, about +7.3%,"
" outside the “within 1%” range (:numref:`tab-mixed-timestep`). \\ For H₂ "
"in double precision, the control with half the time step also agreed "
"within statistical error, but this does not guarantee convergence of the "
"mixed-precision pressures. \\ Even differences of less than 1% vary with "
"calculation settings for precision and constraints, so we do not "
"interpret them as differences in the properties of the gases. \\ The "
"values and control conditions are documented in :doc:`reproduction`."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:142
msgid "分子の質量と運動エネルギー"
msgstr "Molecular Mass and Kinetic Energy"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:144
msgid "理想気体では、圧力と分子の重心運動の関係を、分子1個の質量を :math:`m` として\\ 次のように書けます。"
msgstr ""
"For an ideal gas, the relationship between pressure and molecular center-"
"of-mass motion, where :math:`m` denotes the mass of one molecule, \\ is "
"given by"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:147
msgid ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"P&=\\frac{1}{3}\\frac{N}{V}m\\langle v_{\\mathrm{COM}}^2\\rangle,\\\\\n"
"m\\langle v_{\\mathrm{COM}}^2\\rangle&=3k_{\\mathrm B}T.\n"
"\\end{aligned}"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"P&=\\frac{1}{3}\\frac{N}{V}m\\langle v_{\\mathrm{COM}}^2\\rangle,\\\\\n"
"m\\langle v_{\\mathrm{COM}}^2\\rangle&=3k_{\\mathrm B}T.\n"
"\\end{aligned}"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:154
msgid "周期境界のセルには壁がありませんが、仮想的な面を横切る運動量の流れとしても同じ式を考えることができます。"
msgstr ""
"Although the cell with periodic boundary conditions has no walls, the "
"same equation can be understood in terms of momentum flux across an "
"imaginary surface."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:156
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"質量が大きくなると、同じ温度での速さの二乗は小さくなります。\\ この二つを掛けた量は一定なので、式を合わせると\\ "
":math:`P=Nk_{\\mathrm B}T/V` となり、質量は式から消えます。\\ "
"重い分子がゆっくり動くことが、同じ温度でほぼ同じ圧力になることと両立するのです。"
msgstr ""
"At the same temperature, a larger mass means a lower mean squared speed. "
"\\ The product of the two is constant, so combining the equations gives "
"\\ :math:`P=Nk_{\\mathrm B}T/V` and the mass cancels. \\ This is how "
"heavier molecules can move more slowly and still give nearly the same "
"pressure at the same temperature."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:161
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"この説明は、分子間の力を無視できる希薄な気体についての近似です。\\ GROMACSの圧力には分子間力や拘束力の寄与も含まれます [1]_ 。\\"
" また、分子の回転や変角の運動は、分子全体の並進と区別しなければなりません。\\ "
"全体の温度の表示だけでは、これらの間に熱が十分行き渡ったかは分かりません。\\ その例を次の :numref:`{number}. {name} "
"<gas-five-thermostat>` で示します。"
msgstr ""
"This explanation is an approximation for a dilute gas whose "
"intermolecular forces can be neglected. \\ The GROMACS pressure also "
"includes contributions from intermolecular and constraint forces [1]_. \\"
" Molecular rotation and bending must also be distinguished from "
"translation of the molecule as a whole. \\ The displayed overall "
"temperature alone does not tell whether heat has been sufficiently "
"distributed among these motions. \\ An example is shown in the next "
"section, :numref:`{number}. {name} <gas-five-thermostat>`."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:170
msgid "温度制御"
msgstr "Temperature Control"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:172
msgid ""
"第1回のArでは、Quloudの既定の温度制御で、全体の温度を一定に保つV-rescaleを使いました。\\ 同じV-"
"rescaleでH₂・N₂・O₂・CO₂を計算すると、CO₂では全体の温度が約273 Kでも、重心の速さは約440〜443 "
"m/sで理論値より約12%速く、圧力も約1.27 barになりました。\\ "
"希薄な気体では分子どうしの衝突がまれなため、並進と回転（CO₂では変角も）の間で熱が十分行き渡っていないと考えられます。\\ "
"このように、全体の温度が設定値に近くても、分子の並進が同じ温度になっているとは限りません。分子の気体では重心の速さも確かめる必要があります。\\ "
"そこで今回は、各原子に熱浴を作用させる確率的動力学（SD）を使いました。\\ V-rescaleで計算した速さと圧力は :numref:`tab-"
"vrescale-reference` に、温度も含む数値は配布データの ``vrescale_reference.csv`` に載せています。"
msgstr ""
"For Ar in Part 1, we used V-rescale, Quloud’s default temperature "
"control, which keeps the overall temperature constant. \\ When we "
"calculated H₂, N₂, O₂, and CO₂ with the same V-rescale, the center-of-"
"mass speed of CO₂ was about 440–443 m/s, roughly 12% above the "
"theoretical value, even though the overall temperature was about 273 K, "
"and the pressure reached about 1.27 bar. \\ Collisions between molecules "
"are rare in a dilute gas, so heat is likely not sufficiently distributed "
"between translation and rotation (and, for CO₂, bending). \\ Thus, even "
"when the overall temperature is close to the set value, the translation "
"of the molecules is not necessarily at the same temperature. For "
"molecular gases, the center-of-mass speed also needs to be checked. \\ We"
" therefore used stochastic dynamics (SD), which applies a heat bath to "
"each atom. \\ The speeds and pressures calculated with V-rescale are "
"listed in :numref:`tab-vrescale-reference`, and the values including "
"temperatures are in ``vrescale_reference.csv`` in the distributed data."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:179
msgid ""
"今回のSDは緩和時間0.1 psの強い熱浴を使っています。\\ "
"速さの分布を比べる数値実験であり、実際の分子の飛び方や衝突時間を再現する計算としては使いません。"
msgstr ""
"The SD calculations used a strong heat bath with a relaxation time of 0.1"
" ps. \\ This numerical experiment compares speed distributions. It is not"
" intended to reproduce the actual motion or collision times of real "
"molecules."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:183
msgid "この数値実験から分かること"
msgstr "What the Numerical Experiment Shows"

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:185
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"分子の重心の二乗平均平方根速度は、5種類とも理想気体の理論値 :math:`\\sqrt{3RT/M}` "
"と0.1%以内で一致しました。最も軽いH₂は、最も重いCO₂の約4.7倍の速さで動きます。ただし、これは熱浴が熱平衡に近づけた速度分布から分子全体の運動を取り出した結果で、分子どうしの衝突だけでこの関係が生まれることを示したものではありません。"
msgstr ""
"The root-mean-square speed of the molecular center of mass agreed with "
"the theoretical ideal gas value :math:`\\sqrt{3RT/M}` to within 0.1% for "
"all five gases. The lightest gas, H₂, moves about 4.7 times as fast as "
"the heaviest, CO₂. However, this result was obtained by extracting the "
"motion of whole molecules from a velocity distribution that the heat bath"
" brought close to thermal equilibrium; it does not show that this "
"relationship arises from collisions between molecules alone."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:186
msgid ""
"同じ数の分子を同じ温度・体積に入れると、採用した時間刻みでは、5種類とも圧力が理想気体の予測（1 "
"atm）から1%以内でした。重い分子はゆっくり動くので、分子1個の質量と速さの二乗の積は質量によらず、圧力も質量によりません。"
msgstr ""
"When the same number of molecules was placed at the same temperature and "
"volume, the pressure of all five gases was within 1% of the ideal gas "
"prediction (1 atm) at the time steps we adopted. Because heavier "
"molecules move more slowly, the product of the mass of a molecule and the"
" square of its speed does not depend on the mass, and neither does the "
"pressure."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:187
msgid "気体ごとの1%未満の圧力差は、時間刻みや計算精度で変わるため、物性の差としては扱いません。また、分子の気体では、全体の温度だけでなく分子の並進の速さも確かめる必要があります。"
msgstr ""
"Pressure differences of less than 1% between gases change with the time "
"step and calculation precision, so we do not treat them as differences in"
" physical properties. Also, for molecular gases, not only the overall "
"temperature but also the translational speed of the molecules needs to be"
" checked."

#: ../../gas_laws/five_gases_avogadro.rst:189
msgid ""
"今回の結果は、登録モデルによる希薄な古典気体の数値実験です。\\ "
"H₂の量子力学的な回転・振動や、実在気体の高精度な状態方程式まで再現するものではありません。\\ "
"さらに圧縮した条件は、相互作用やモデルの限界も強く出る、別の実験として調べる必要があります。"
msgstr ""
"These results describe a numerical experiment on dilute classical gases "
"using the registered models. \\ The calculations do not reproduce quantum"
" rotation or vibration in H₂ or provide a high-precision equation of "
"state for real gases. \\ More compressed conditions require a separate "
"experiment, because interactions and the limitations of the models become"
" more pronounced."

